::node[deploy_to_prod]
->[:role=skill]
->[:scope=all]
->[:keywords=deploy, production, release, ship]
->[:requires=run_tests]
::dense
deploy|prod|requires green tests|tag release|push
::warning
Never deploy to production with failing tests or uncommitted changes.
::full
Deploying to production is a multi-step process that must be done carefully.
First ensure the working tree is clean and all tests pass. Then tag the release
with a semantic version, build the artifact, and push it through the deploy
pipeline. Monitor the rollout and be ready to roll back if health checks fail.
This full block is intentionally verbose to represent real skill content that
would otherwise be dumped into the context window on every single load.
::steps
1. Verify the working tree is clean.
2. Run the full test suite and confirm it is green.
3. Tag the release with a semantic version.
4. Build and push the artifact through the deploy pipeline.
5. Monitor health checks and roll back on failure.
::code[lang=bash]
git status --porcelain
pytest -q
git tag -a "v$VERSION" -m "release"
::assertion
tests_pass: the full test suite exits 0
clean_tree: git status reports no uncommitted changes
::edges
->[:requires] run_tests

::node[run_tests]
->[:role=skill]
->[:scope=all]
->[:keywords=test, pytest, verify]
::dense
run|pytest -q|all green before proceeding
::full
Run the complete automated test suite and confirm every single test passes
before relying on the result. Treat any failure as a hard stop signal.
::steps
1. Install dev dependencies.
2. Run pytest quietly.
3. Confirm zero failures.

::node[secret_rotation]
->[:role=skill]
->[:scope=orchestrator]
->[:keywords=secret, rotate, credentials]
::dense
rotate|secrets|orchestrator-only
::full
Rotate production secrets on a fixed cadence. Restricted to the orchestrator
role because it touches privileged credential stores.
